-- title:
--   Eq. (2.10): $\Gamma(E_{i,j}) = \mathrm{CNOT}_{j,i}$ and $\Gamma(\mathrm{SL}(n;\mathbb F_2)) = G_n$
-- statement:
--   For $1\le i\ne j\le n$ let $E_{i,j}=I_n+e_ie_j^{\mathsf T}\in\mathrm{SL}(n;\mathbb F_2)$. Then $E_{i,j}x = x + x_j e_i$, so under the representation $\Gamma$ of Eq. (2.8)
--   $$
--   \Gamma(E_{i,j}) = \mathrm{CNOT}_{j,i}\qquad\text{(control } j\text{, target } i\text{)},
--   $$
--   and the image of $\Gamma$ is the CNOT group:
--   $$
--   \Gamma(\mathrm{SL}(n;\mathbb F_2)) = G_n .
--   $$
--
--   This identifies $\mathrm{SL}(n;\mathbb F_2)$, through $\Gamma$, with the group generated by all CNOT gates; it is how Kassabov's generators of $\mathrm{SL}(3s;\mathbb F_2)$ become CNOT circuits.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $E_{i,j}$ is Mathlib's `Matrix.transvection i j 1`; $\Gamma$ takes values in permutations of $\{0,1\}^n$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: Γ : SL(n; F₂) → U(2ⁿ) → Γ : SL(n; F₂) →* permutations of {0,1}ⁿ (its unitary is the permutation matrix); reason: the paper defines Γ(g) by permuting basis states; same map
--   - encoding: qubits labelled 1, …, n → qubits labelled 0, …, n − 1 (paper qubit p is index (p − 1) mod n); reason: Lean indexing convention; same gates
-- source:
--   Anshu–Balasubramanian–Haferkamp–Harrow–Tan, Depth-1 expanders on the unitary group and applications, arXiv:2609.01605 (held version, sha256 3c3f8513…aebfd87), Eq. (2.10) and the sentence after it, p.7

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MITMSynthesis_Gate
import Definitions.Def_DepthOneQExp_cnotPerm
import Definitions.Def_DepthOneQExp_cnotGroup
import Definitions.Def_DepthOneQExp_gamma

namespace DepthOneQExp

/-- Eq. (2.10) and the sentence after it (Anshu–Balasubramanian–Haferkamp–Harrow–Tan, *Depth-1
expanders on the unitary group and applications*, arXiv:2609.01605, held version sha256
3c3f8513…aebfd87, p.7): for `i ≠ j`, the elementary matrix `E_{i,j} = I_n + e_i e_jᵀ` acts as the
gate `CNOT_{j,i}` (control `j`, target `i`), `Γ(E_{i,j}) = CNOT_{j,i}`; and
`Γ(SL(n; 𝔽₂)) = G_n`, the group generated by all CNOT gates on `n` qubits.

**Formalization Note** `E_{i,j}` is Mathlib's `Matrix.transvection i j 1`; 0-based coordinates. -/
theorem gamma_cnot_and_range (n : ℕ) :
    (∀ (i j : Fin n) (h : i ≠ j),
      gamma n ⟨Matrix.transvection i j 1, Matrix.det_transvection_of_ne i j h 1⟩ =
        cnotPerm n j i) ∧
    (gamma n).range = cnotGroup n := by sorry

end DepthOneQExp
